Here's how to implement this in .NET MAUI Shell:

**1. Custom "Cancel" back button & intercept hardware/gesture back:**

```csharp
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    public EditProductPage()
    {
        InitializeComponent();

        // Custom back button text
        Shell.SetBackButtonBehavior(this, new BackButtonBehavior
        {
            TextOverride = "Cancel",
            Command = new Command(async () => await TryGoBack())
        });
    }

    // Intercept hardware/swipe back (Android back button, iOS swipe)
    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            // Fire-and-forget the confirmation; return true to cancel navigation
            _ = TryGoBack();
            return true;
        }
        return false; // allow default behavior
    }

    private async Task TryGoBack()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!leave) return; // user chose "Stay"
        }

        await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    }
}
```

**2. Track unsaved changes in your form:**

```csharp
private void OnEntryTextChanged(object sender, TextChangedEventArgs e)
{
    _hasUnsavedChanges = true;
}
```

**Key points:**

- **`BackButtonBehavior`** — replaces the shell back arrow with a "Cancel" text button and routes taps through your command.
- **`OnBackButtonPressed()`** — intercepts Android hardware back and returns `true` to cancel default navigation.
- **iOS swipe-back gesture** — `BackButtonBehavior.Command` handles this since setting it disables the default iOS pop. If you still see issues, add `Shell.SetPresentationMode` or disable the gesture via a platform-specific handler.

> ⚠️ `OnBackButtonPressed` only fires on Android. On iOS/Mac, the `BackButtonBehavior.Command` is the primary interception point.
